Package: breedtools
Title: Design and Analysis of Augmented Plant Breeding Trials
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Christiano", "Simoes", email = "ccsimoes263@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Generates and analyzes field trial designs for early-generation
    plant breeding. Creates augmented row-column designs with replicated
    checks (Federer, Nair and Raghavarao (1975) <doi:10.2307/2529426>) and
    multi-location augmented partially replicated (p-rep) designs (Williams,
    Piepho and Whitaker (2011) <doi:10.1002/bimj.201000102>), draws field
    maps, and exports field books in 'Breedbase' format. Analyses give
    analysis of variance tables with degrees of freedom estimable from the
    observed plots and spatially adjusted entry means (best linear unbiased
    estimates) with standard errors. Also loads 'Breedbase' phenotype files,
    checks residual variance homogeneity across environments with Hartley's
    Fmax test (Hartley (1950) <doi:10.1093/biomet/37.3-4.308>), and groups
    environments by genotype-by-environment interaction (Lin (1982)
    <doi:10.1007/BF00276251>).
